$date
	Tue Oct 27 15:00:00 2026
$end
$version
	QuestaSim 2023.3_1
$end
$comment
	A Questa 2023 VCD writes the value of an integer (an enum variable's code) without its b and glued to its id
	code: 00000000000000000000000000000001A& is 1 of A&, not 0 of a code 0000…1A& no $var declares. Read as the
	digits of the variable's width, then its code (nib: a code that starts with a digit, 0a); a b value and a
	bit as usual between them.
$end
$timescale
	1ns
$end
$scope module tb $end
$var reg 1 ! clk $end
$var integer 32 A& state $end
$var integer 32 "9 next $end
$var reg 4 0a nib [3:0] $end
$upscope $end
$enddefinitions $end
#0
$dumpvars
0!
00000000000000000000000000000000A&
00000000000000000000000000000001"9
00010a
$end
#5
1!
00000000000000000000000000000001A&
00000000000000000000000000000010"9
#10
0!
b10 A&
#15
1!
00000000000000000000000000000011A&
0000000000000000000000000000xxxx"9
11110a
#20
0!
